<h2><a name=3D"_e6420iimgg33"></a><span lang=3DEN>Helping</span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>Up to three other player characters or=
 NPCs
can help you with a dice roll. Each person helping gives you +1 die, but th=
ey
need to be in a position to actually support your action.</span></p>

<h2><a name=3D"_n61mwyfckdq8"></a><span lang=3DEN>Pushing</span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>If you fail a skill test, or if you ne=
ed more
successes, you can choose to push the roll -re-roll all of the dice (except=
 any
sixes, should there be any). After pushing a roll, you suffer Condition.</s=
pan></p>

<h2><a name=3D"_56dsk9l9r6at"></a><span lang=3DEN>Swapping Initiative</span=
></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>You and another player character can c=
hoose to
swap initiative during combat. You may only swap at the start of the round.=
</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>In combat, extra successes can be used=
 to
outmaneuver the opponent, forcing them to swap initiative with you. If the
opponent has not yet had their turn, they won&#8217;t get a turn this round=
.</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'text-indent:.5in'><span lang=3DEN>Note: Spent=
 fast
actions still count as spent</span></p>

<h2><a name=3D"_rne7u9fp0a92"></a><span lang=3DEN>Slow &amp; Fast Actions</=
span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>You can perform two actions per round,=
 one
slow and one fast. If you want, you can perform a fast action instead of yo=
ur
slow one and thus get two fast actions that round.</span></p>

