<h2><a name=3D"_z6200qcbwoi"></a><span lang=3DEN>Attacking</span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>Unarmed attacks are performed with a F=
ORCE
skill test. When armed with a melee weapon, use CLOSE COMBAT. For ranged
attacks, use RANGED COMBAT. If the test succeeds, the target suffers a numb=
er
of physical Conditions equal to the damage rating of the weapon. For each e=
xtra
success you rolled beyond the first, the target suffers an additional
Condition.</span></p>

<h2><a name=3D"_w6r69l9d281b"></a><span lang=3DEN>Dodging &amp; Parrying</s=
pan></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>When attacked, you can use a fast acti=
on to
parry in close combat, or dodge a ranged attack. You can do this even if it=
 is
not your turn. To dodge, test AGILITY. To parry, test FORCE or CLOSE COMBAT
depending on if you are armed. Each success eliminates one success from the
enemy&#8217;s attack. If you eliminate all successes, the attack misses. You
must declare a dodge or parry before the enemy rolls for the attack.</span>=
</p>

<h2><a name=3D"_ihg3tn0p0k1"></a><span lang=3DEN>Conditions</span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>When you suffer a Condition, you can c=
hoose
any Condition you like from the relevant type (physical or mental). When you
have checked off all three physical or mental Conditions and suffer another=
 one
of the same type, you are Broken. This means that you are incapacitated or =
have
suffered a breakdown, and are unable to act. If Broken by physical Conditio=
ns,
you risk dying.</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>Once broken, you suffer a critical inj=
ury
which will be either an affliction or an insight</span></p>

