</v:shape><![endif]--><![if !vml]><img width=3D384 height=3D220
src=3D"VaesenPH_files/image008.gif" align=3Dleft hspace=3D12 vspace=3D12 v:=
shapes=3D"image16.png"><![endif]></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>The newly-appointed police chief, Oscar
Stierna, is one of the few people in the force who cannot be bought. He is
trying to purge his organization of corruption. Some officers idealize him =
and
have stopped working with shady elements. Others hate him.</span></p>

<h3><a name=3D"_ahk0owms7s1d"></a><span lang=3DEN>THE POORHOUSE </span></h3>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>Begging, vagrancy, and poverty are ill=
egal.
Those who are found guilty of such crimes are confined to poorhouses.
Upsala&#8217;s poorhouse, located in Kamphavet Square, is packed with paupe=
rs,
reduced to poverty by years of crop failure. The master of the poorhouse is
Doctor Per Dubb. Together with the local police force, Dubb runs an extensi=
ve
network of informants with the aim of tracking down and apprehending thieves
and beggars. Those who are forced to live at the poorhouse lead miserable l=
ives
plagued by starvation, lice, and abuse.</span><!--[if gte vml 1]><v:shape i=
