 mso-wrap-distance-top:9pt;mso-wrap-distance-right:9pt;
 mso-wrap-distance-bottom:9pt;mso-position-horizontal:absolute;
 mso-position-horizontal-relative:text;mso-position-vertical:absolute;
 mso-position-vertical-relative:text'>
 <v:imagedata src=3D"VaesenPH_files/image053.png" o:title=3D""/>
 <w:wrap type=3D"square"/>
</v:shape><![endif]--><![if !vml]><img width=3D294 height=3D1
src=3D"VaesenPH_files/image054.gif" align=3Dleft hspace=3D12 vspace=3D12 v:=
shapes=3D"image24.png"><![endif]></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>In addition to medical and mental care=
, you
can heal your own Conditions by resting or engaging in an activity that
provides relaxation. Summarize what happens or play a short scene. If alone,
you heal one physical or mental Condition of your choice. If the scene invo=
lves
another person, NPC or player character, or your memento (your memento can =
only
be used once per session) you heal two Conditions. </span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>Resting can only be done once per day,=
 and the
Broken Condition cannot be healed this way. If multiple characters are
participating in the same scene, they can all heal Conditions from it.</spa=
n></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<h2><a name=3D"_p7ndy8jj3os4"></a><span lang=3DEN>SERVICES AND ESTABLISHMEN=
TS </span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>Finally, it is possible to purchase me=
dical
attention or heal Conditions at a local doctor&#8217;s office, by recuperat=
ing
at some finer establishment, traveling lavishly, or resting at a nice hoste=
l or
hotel. It counts as resting (above) but must be bought with a roll for
Resources.</span></p>

<h1><a name=3D"_oz1eb53giw6"></a><span lang=3DEN>GEAR </span></h1>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>You always have access to your persona=
l gear,
but during a mystery you may also need to procure weapons, armor, or other
equipment. Such items are called temporary gear and are usually acquired du=
ring
the mystery&#8217;s preparation phase, before leaving your headquarters, bu=
t it
can also be done on site as the story unfolds. </span></p>

<h2><a name=3D"_jrk9o6tg5h4"></a><span lang=3DEN>PREPARATORY GEAR </span></=
h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>Items have a cost level from 1 to 5 th=
at
indicates how easy it is to acquire. Equipment is mostly obtained through
contacts and status, represented by your Resources value. Your party is
expected to procure temporary gear for the expedition at the start of the
mystery, before you head out. It is part of the preparation phase. </span><=
/p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>Each player rolls the number of dice i=
ndicated
by their character&#8217;s Resources value. The number of successes is used=
 to
purchase temporary gear &#8211; for example, an item with cost 1 costs one
success, while another with level 3 costs three successes. </span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><!--[if gte vml 1]><v:shape id=3D"image17.png" o:spid=
=3D"_x0000_s1026"
 type=3D"#_x0000_t75" style=3D'position:absolute;margin-left:198.75pt;margi=
n-top:17.05pt;
 width:268.95pt;height:287.65pt;z-index:251664384;visibility:visible;
 mso-wrap-style:square;mso-wrap-distance-left:9pt;mso-wrap-distance-top:9pt;
 mso-wrap-distance-right:9pt;mso-wrap-distance-bottom:9pt;
 mso-position-horizontal:absolute;mso-position-horizontal-relative:text;
 mso-position-vertical:absolute;mso-position-vertical-relative:text'>
 <v:imagedata src=3D"VaesenPH_files/image055.png" o:title=3D""/>
 <w:wrap type=3D"square"/>
</v:shape><![endif]--><![if !vml]><img width=3D359 height=3D1
src=3D"VaesenPH_files/image056.gif" align=3Dleft hspace=3D12 vspace=3D12 v:=
shapes=3D"image17.png"><![endif]></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>You can donate successes to each other=
, or add
them together to purchase more expensive items and decide among yourselves =
who
will carry them, regardless of whose successes paid for them. </span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>Each player may also decide to move po=
ints
from their free Capital, but will then have less money to spend during the
mystery (see below). In addition, certain Upgrades to the Society&#8217;s
headquarters can help you acquire temporary gear at the start of a mystery.=
 </span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<h2><a name=3D"_catvyeukyavh"></a><span lang=3DEN>SHOPPING DURING THE MYSTE=
RY </span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>Once on site, the PCs are expected to =
have
money, status, or goods that correspond to their respective living standard=
s.
When bartering with a non-player character who is reluctant to part with an
item, you make an opposed roll for <b>MANIPULATION </b>and add a bonus base=
d on
your living standard (see the table above). An item is bought by achieving a
number of successes equal to or greater than the item&#8217;s cost. </span>=
</p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>For normal purchases, from someone wil=
ling to
sell at a fixed price, the Resources value is rolled to see how much money =
(or
what promise of future payment) the player character is good for. </span></=
p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>Rich individuals can automatically pur=
chase
equipment during an ongoing mystery by spending Capital (see the table abov=
e).
Spent Capital is used up until the next mystery and can be used instead of a
success test or added to increase the number of successes. </span></p>

<h2><a name=3D"_drbaem6wba07"></a><span lang=3DEN>LOSING GEAR </span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>All temporary gear is lost at the end =
of the
mystery. It&#8217;s assumed to be lost, returned or sold in the time that
passes before the next mystery. This also goes for temporary gear found or
stolen during the mystery. Only a character&#8217;s personal gear remains f=
rom
one mystery to the next. However, Upgrades of the Society&#8217;s headquart=
ers
can allow for saving some temporary gear from one mystery to the next.</spa=
n></p>

<h2><a name=3D"_gjnfbr73omgc"></a><span lang=3DEN>ARMOR AND COVER </span></=
h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>You can wear armor to protect yourself=
 from
attacks. Armor gives you a Protection value. When hit by an attack, you roll
the number of dice indicated by the armor&#8217;s Protection. Each success
reduces the damage by 1. Wearing armor also makes you clumsy and imparts a
penalty to <b>AGILITY</b>. </span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>The table above lists the Protection v=
alue,
the number of dice you must subtract from <b>AGILITY </b>tests, and the cos=
t. </span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>An example of light armor is a leather
cuirass. A medium armor could be to wear a helmet and a chain mail shirt, w=
hile
heavy armor could mean putting on an old suit of plate mail armor before yo=
ur
encounter with a fearsome vaesen. </span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>In combat you can also choose to take =
cover
behind walls, barriers, or parts of the terrain to avoid getting hit by ran=
ged
weapons. This requires a fast action. While in cover you may also dodge att=
acks
as usual. </span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>The cover gives you a Protection value=
. You
roll the number of dice indicated by the Protection value, and each success
reduces the damage of the attack by 1. Cover does not protect against attac=
ks
from enemies in the same zone as you, since the enemy can go around or over=
 the
cover and attack you. An exception to this rule is explosions; cover protec=
ts
against explosions even in the same zone.</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN style=3D'mso-no-proof:yes'><!--[if gte=
 vml 1]><v:shape
 id=3D"image34.png" o:spid=3D"_x0000_i1031" type=3D"#_x0000_t75" style=3D'w=
idth:468pt;
 height:153.75pt;visibility:visible;mso-wrap-style:square'>
 <v:imagedata src=3D"VaesenPH_files/image057.png" o:title=3D""/>
</v:shape><![endif]--><![if !vml]><img border=3D0 width=3D624 height=3D205
src=3D"VaesenPH_files/image058.gif" v:shapes=3D"image34.png"><![endif]></sp=
an></p>

<h2><a name=3D"_lesudis4cet9"></a><span lang=3DEN>GEAR, WEAPONS AND SERVICE=
S </span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>Tools, weapons, and other items help y=
ou by
adding a bonus to your skill tests. The bonus indicates the number of extra
dice you may roll. You may also visit various establishments or purchase
services that can make things easier during the mystery or serve as a place=
 for
healing Conditions. Each service applies to the whole party, rather than any
individual character. </span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN>The weapons tables show a list of weap=
ons the
characters might use. Damage indicates how many Conditions the opponent suf=
fers
if hit. Range shows which zones you can reach with your attack. Range 0&#82=
11;1
means you can attack enemies in your zone and adjacent zones, while 1&#8211=
;3
means you can attack enemies one, two, or three zones away, but not enemies=
 in
your own zone. Bonus indicates how many dice you may add to your success te=
st
when trying to hit your enemy. Skill shows which skill to roll for.</span><=
/p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN style=3D'mso-no-proof:yes'><!--[if gte=
 vml 1]><v:shape
 id=3D"image14.png" o:spid=3D"_x0000_i1030" type=3D"#_x0000_t75" style=3D'w=
idth:427.5pt;
 height:235.5pt;visibility:visible;mso-wrap-style:square'>
